/STR 92a9941c raw
"A good pair of Sancho's saddlebags. Inside there is: "
/STR 7a5859a5
A long lance, old and fearsome, in that order.
/STR 6ec5e1be
An old leather buckler, to cover yourself from the blows you fail to dodge.
/STR d125c91e
Your great-grandfathers' sword. It cuts, if you insist.
/STR 66d3b2c9
Some iron bars, thin and strong. They would do to strengthen something.
/STR 6bf37a2c
The covers of a book by Feliciano de Silva. Good printer's pasteboard.
/STR 7202e8b7
A small key, the kind for a chest.
/STR 86ad91d6
Your savings: a few ducats you scraped together by selling one thing and pawning another.
/STR 6b7fb63d
A clean shirt. The innkeeper said knights carried them.
/STR a25704cf
A linen sheet, long and strong. Your niece embroidered it.
/STR 4b37ff6d
A ladder made of strips of sheet. It will hold. Probably.
/STR 783e1f85
The iron tip of your lance. The only thing that survived the giant.
/STR 6a87b5ab
A dry oak branch, long and almost straight. With a tip, it would be a lance.
/STR 5e6da8d5
Notebooks written in Arabic characters. There is a drawing of a very thin knight and a very fat squire.
/STR f61fcfc0
Rosemary. It smells of hillside and of remedy.
/STR 58c47d31
Salt. Salty.
/STR 206f049d
Olive oil. Good stuff, for an inn.
/STR e009a0e2
Red wine. Or so the innkeeper says.
/STR 2f555679
A tin flask, the kind for keeping oil in.
/STR f3c58e01
The balsam of Fierabras. A single drop, your books say, cures every wound. It smells awful.
/STR d2d4eb70
The helmet of Mambrino. It is of gold (or of brass), half the headpiece is missing and it has a notch for the beard. Sancho says it is a barber's basin. Sancho knows nothing about helmets.
/STR ef2ffcb0
A richly bound memorandum book. Good for writing in.
/STR 83cc8571
A strip of shirt with eleven knots, one bigger than the rest. Your rosary.
/STR c7f36475
You see nothing special.
/STR c28d8686
Where? The only thing you can put things into is the SADDLEBAGS.
/STR 694408c0
You have nothing to take it out of.
/STR 89c8380d
The dapple is Sancho's. And Sancho is very particular about it.
/STR bc47ebd2
You are already mounted. As far as you know.
/STR c41b23e6
Rocinante is not here.
/STR 4289bb2b
Mount a nameless nag? No knight errant would. First think of a name worthy of him.
/STR b6844d61
In your state, you couldn't even climb onto a chair.
/STR d5ace7c2
You mount Rocinante. He sighs; so do you, but with joy.
/STR a29f1e7a
You are not mounted.
/STR 78ddf5aa
You dismount from Rocinante, who is grateful.
/STR 2a30e058
You insult the air. The air, luckily, carries no sword.
/STR 9c825724
You talk to yourself, as usual. (To talk to someone: SAY TO SANCHO "HELLO")
/STR 35b5a9c6
It smells of La Mancha: of thyme, of dust and of garlic.
/STR 8b337c51
This is no time to sleep. A knight errant sleeps little and badly.
/STR 0649069c
You have nothing to eat. Knights errant, according to your books, hardly eat.
/STR 417ba175
You have nothing to drink. Sancho has the wineskin, but he keeps an eye on it.
/STR 6759f599
There is nobody here worthy of your lance. For now.
/STR ccad703d
You have no lance to wield.
/STR c36c0a7e
You commend yourself to your lady Dulcinea. She, in El Toboso, has no idea.
/STR a9744364
There is nothing to read here. More's the pity.
/STR 861b0cb2
You can't open that.
/STR f5b72678
There is no need to close anything.
/STR a1b97633
You cut two capers in the air. Nobody applauds.
/STR 03bc2254
You hear the wind of La Mancha. And Sancho, chewing something.
/STR 13aafd0a
You search and don't find. Like nearly everybody.
/STR 9b3ad048
You are already up. More or less.
/STR b762882c
Better not.
/STR f9f00070
Sancho doesn't want it. He wants islands.
/STR 682bf0fc
There is nobody to give it to.
/STR e68a7c7a
There is nobody here to pay. So much the better for you.
/STR 63a6b697
Nothing is sold here.
/STR 3ea27fdb
You don't know how to make that.
/STR 087782bf
There is no need to test that.
/STR 51812e4f
Better not break that.
/STR 3c0ebb4e
There is nowhere to tie that.
/STR 3be2bbbe
There is nothing to untie.
/STR be9936e8
You have nothing to write in, or on.
/STR 8f56d3d6
One, two, three... You lose count.
/STR 7ef71d21
Not here. There is a place for every madness.
/STR b2400350
That is as clean as it is ever going to be.
/STR 5f8415ec
Arms are watched in a chapel. Or in a yard, if the chapel has been pulled down.
/STR e0d1eef2
You think. It hurts a little.
/STR 6d388cce
There is nothing to cut.
/STR 58f1cc48
You are already awake. Or so you think.
